  "final_text": "Both the dashboard and the rule now exist. The rule is enabled and its first run succeeded.\n\n**Data view:** `kibana_sample_data_logs` uses `timestamp` as its time field. Useful fields are `response` (string, with `response.keyword` for exact matching), `bytes`, `clientip`, `geo.dest`, `extension`, `url`, and `machine.os`. I could not run ad-hoc aggregations here. The console proxy, `/internal/search/es`, and `/internal/search/esql` are all disabled on this Kibana, so I could not check how many 5xx responses the data actually contains.\n\n**Dashboard \"EFF-57282eb0 Web logs overview\"** (id `f2f224bb-de9d-40de-ad96-997bbf6e957c`), five panels:\n- Total requests (count)\n- 5xx responses (count, filtered to `response.keyword` starting with `5`)\n- Average response bytes\n- Requests over time (line, date histogram on `timestamp`)\n- 5xx responses over time (line, same 5xx filter)\n\nThe first PUT of the dashboard stored the 5xx filter with an empty query, so I corrected it and updated the dashboard in place. The stored filters now match the intended prefix query.\n\n**Rule \"EFF-57282eb0 5xx spike\"** (id `70d174d2-bd6e-44be-8e19-311143ec2003`):\n- Type: Elasticsearch query (`.es-query`), consumer `stackAlerts`\n- Index `kibana_sample_data_logs`, time field `timestamp`\n- Query: `response.keyword` prefix `5`\n- Condition: count > 10 over a 5-minute window\n- Schedule: every 1m\n- Enabled, no actions attached\n\nDecisions I made that you may want to change:\n- \"5xx\" means any status starting with 5, which covers 500\u2013599.\n- The rule has no connector, so it records alerts but sends no notifications. Adding an action would make it notify someone.\n- I tagged the rule `EFF-57282eb0`.\n\nScratch request bodies are in the scratchpad directory, not the project.",
